ONE LINE: forms are kant fields laid out by setFrame and drawn by a kant walk over a short C++ floor, to a bitmap and to a PDF. 3 of 21 forms draw.

/*****************************************************************************
    Description
*****************************************************************************/
A form is a define block: a tree of fields (window, body, panels, controls) whose attributes are a little language, not assignments. Nothing fires at define.
    Layout   setFrame gives every field a frame from x y width height, down, across and space.
    Draw     the walk draws each field in the order fill, image, border, text; one floor call each.
    Event    a click selects the field, fires its action, then its attribute actions left to right; bubbling goes up the enclosing fields. Not built.
Tony is the form designer: once the attributes are fleshed out he finishes the IncantForms forms himself, using the tools.

